# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env* is gitignored, so real values never
# reach the repository. At deployment set the same values on the Cloudflare
# Worker: the three Brevo ones as secrets, NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL as a build
# variable (Workers Builds → Settings → Variables and Secrets).

# --- Enquiry form → email via Brevo -----------------------------------------
# The form on /contact posts to /api/enquiry, which sends one email per
# enquiry through Brevo (free plan, 300/day). All three are read on the SERVER
# only — the key in the page source would let anyone send as us.
#
# 1. brevo.com → free account. The address you sign up with becomes a verified
#    sender; add others under Senders, Domains & Dedicated IPs → Senders.
# 2. Account menu → SMTP & API → API Keys → Generate a new API key. Shown once.
# 3. ENQUIRY_FROM must be a verified sender. ENQUIRY_TO is where enquiries
#    land — the business Gmail. Recipients need no verification.
BREVO_API_KEY=
ENQUIRY_FROM=
ENQUIRY_TO=

# --- Site -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The real domain. Canonical URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt and the
# LocalBusiness structured data all build off this. Decided: aadienterprise.in
# (not yet bought). The value below and the fallback in src/lib/site-url.ts
# still say .com and are switched once the domain is attached.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://aadienterprise.com

# --- Sanity ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live site needs NO Sanity credential. Project hhvsb0rp / dataset
# "production" is public, and the build reads published content anonymously.
# These two are baked into src/sanity/client.ts; set them only to point a
# build at a different project or dataset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=hhvsb0rp
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production

# Developer-role token for the Sanity CLI ONLY — deploying the Studio
# (npm run studio:deploy) and seeding (npm run seed). Never set this on the
# host; nothing in the site reads it. Create one at sanity.io/manage → API →
# Tokens, and delete it when the setup work is done.
# SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN=
